 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery** (`docs/decisions/change-delivery-approach.md`). Connected browsers receive committed revisions over self-hosted WebSocket sessions, catching up via revision replay after brief disconnects. Five-second HTTPS polling and a hosted realtime service were rejected in favor of low-latency updates without vendor lock-in or recurring realtime fees, accepting ownership of socket capacity, session management, and reconnect recovery.
